Subject: [PATCH] a switch to leave the recovery install script out

For a device that is not A/B and builds a recovery image, the target files step
always runs make_recovery_patch. With BOARD_USES_FULL_RECOVERY_IMAGE, which
LineageOS turns on, that puts two files into the system image:

    /vendor/bin/install-recovery.sh   writes /vendor/etc/recovery.img over the
                                      recovery partition when its hash differs
    /vendor/etc/recovery.img          LineageOS' recovery, 42 MB

The script is started by the vendor_flash_recovery service when
persist.vendor.recovery_update is true, and the setup wizard and the Updater
offer that switch whenever the script exists.

On ASUS_P00I the recovery partition holds the one tool the tablet can be
repaired with, behind a locked bootloader, and nothing may rewrite it. Not
building a recovery image at all (TARGET_NO_RECOVERY) is not a way out: the
release tools then refuse to make the installable zip.

TARGET_NO_RECOVERY_PATCH skips that one step. The generator of the zip insists
on finding its result, so the switch is also written to misc_info.txt
(no_recovery_patch) for it to accept the absence.
---
diff --git a/core/Makefile b/core/Makefile
index fb655cd..e4971ba 100644
--- a/core/Makefile
+++ b/core/Makefile
@@ -5283,6 +5283,9 @@ endif
 ifeq ($(BOARD_USES_FULL_RECOVERY_IMAGE),true)
 	$(hide) echo "full_recovery_image=true" >> $@
 endif
+ifeq ($(TARGET_NO_RECOVERY_PATCH),true)
+	$(hide) echo "no_recovery_patch=true" >> $@
+endif
 ifdef BUILDING_VENDOR_IMAGE
 	$(hide) echo "board_builds_vendorimage=true" >> $@
 endif
@@ -6016,10 +6019,12 @@ ifneq ($(PRODUCT_SYSTEM_DLKM_BASE_FS_PATH),)
 endif
 ifeq ($(TARGET_OTA_ALLOW_NON_AB),true)
 ifneq ($(INSTALLED_RECOVERYIMAGE_TARGET),)
+ifneq ($(TARGET_NO_RECOVERY_PATCH),true)
 	$(hide) PATH=$(INTERNAL_USERIMAGES_BINARY_PATHS):$$PATH MKBOOTIMG=$(MKBOOTIMG) \
 	    $(MAKE_RECOVERY_PATCH) $(zip_root) $(zip_root)
 endif
 endif
+endif
 ifeq ($(AB_OTA_UPDATER),true)
 	@# When using the A/B updater, include the updater config files in the zip.
 	$(hide) cp $(TOPDIR)system/update_engine/update_engine.conf $(zip_root)/META/update_engine_config.txt
diff --git a/tools/releasetools/non_ab_ota.py b/tools/releasetools/non_ab_ota.py
index 9e4356b..1cc7d81 100644
--- a/tools/releasetools/non_ab_ota.py
+++ b/tools/releasetools/non_ab_ota.py
@@ -156,7 +156,9 @@ def WriteFullOTAPackage(input_zip, output_file):
       metadata=metadata,
       info_dict=OPTIONS.info_dict)
 
-  assert HasRecoveryPatch(input_zip, info_dict=OPTIONS.info_dict)
+  # TARGET_NO_RECOVERY_PATCH: the build left the recovery install script out on purpose.
+  assert (OPTIONS.info_dict.get("no_recovery_patch") == "true" or
+          HasRecoveryPatch(input_zip, info_dict=OPTIONS.info_dict))
 
   # Assertions (e.g. downgrade check, device properties check).
   #ts = target_info.GetBuildProp("ro.build.date.utc")
